  "result": "The cause is in `join_options` (`src/click/formatting.py:319`). It sorts an option's names by prefix length with `reverse=True`, so `--help` lands before `-h`. The existing test at `tests/test_commands.py:188` expects `-h, --help`.\n\nI'm in plan mode, so I haven't edited anything. The plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\the-help-output-looks-linked-penguin.md`.\n\n**Proposed fix:** change line 319 from `rv.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)` to `rv.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])`.\n\n**Verification:** run `pytest tests/test_commands.py tests/test_formatting.py tests/test_options.py`, then check that a `--verbose`/`-v` option prints `-v, --verbose`.\n\nLet me know if you want me to apply it, since plan mode blocks edits. If by \"options\" you meant the order of the options in the list rather than the names within one option, tell me and I'll look at that instead.",
